<title>NETHERLANDS: Nedlloyd to sell Geytenbeek to Marcon.</title>
<headline>Nedlloyd to sell Geytenbeek to Marcon.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch shipping and road transport group Koninklijke Nedlloyd Groep NV said on Monday it would sell its Geytenbeek unit to Marcon Nederland, a unit of Dutch firm Lintzen Group.  </p>
<p>&quot;It is the intention that the transfer be effected as per September 1,&quot; Nedlloyd said in a statement.</p>
<p>Geytenbeek specialises in industrial removals and archive management and employs 140 people.</p>
<p>No financial details were disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
